engine: high fall for final bang, lift only

The intonation rules test for question records and never for bang.
Borrowing the question rise reads patanong, so the bang keeps its
own falling shape and is raised instead: vb70 baseline lift, inflection
untouched, next utterance's own numbers put everything back. Loudness
lives app-side off the same final mark. Mid-sentence bangs untouched.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
diff --git a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c
index fb97f8e..210e1f5 100644
--- a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c
+++ b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthtext.c
@@ -339,6 +339,65 @@ static int utf8ToWestern(const char *text, uint32_t len, char *out,
     return 1;
 }
 
+/* ---- excitement for ! and ? ------------------------------------------ */
+
+/* The engine reads every sentence end the same: hello! comes out flat
+   where ETI shouts it, because the mark never reaches intonation -- the
+   intonation rules test for question records and never for bang, so a
+   final bang takes the declarative defaults. A shout is not a question:
+   borrowing the question rise reads patanong, so the bang keeps its own
+   falling shape and is raised and played louder instead -- a high fall.
+   Mid-sentence bangs, which the rules already shape, are left alone.
+ *
+ * The baseline lift uses the same `vb shape the caller-facing prosody
+   already sends every utterance -- the inflection is never touched --
+   so a malformed one cannot slip in and the next utterance's own
+   numbers put everything back. The loudness half lives app-side, keyed
+   off the same final mark.
+ *
+ * Only the last mark of the text counts, past trailing space and
+   closers, and only for the utterance as a whole. Answers a new buffer
+   holding prefix plus text, or nought when the text ends in anything
+   else. All languages shout. */
+static char *excite_rewrite(const char *text, uint32_t len, uint32_t *newlen)
+{
+    uint32_t end = len;
+    const char *prefix = 0;
+    uint32_t pn = 0;
+    char *out;
+
+    if (text == 0 || len == 0)
+        return 0;
+    while (end > 0) {
+        unsigned char c = (unsigned char)text[end - 1];
+
+        if (c == ' ' || c == '\t' || c == '\n' || c == '\r' || c == '"'
+            || c == '\'' || c == ')' || c == ']' || c == '}')
+            end--;
+        else
+            break;
+    }
+    if (end == 0)
+        return 0;
+    if (text[end - 1] == '!') {
+        prefix = "`vb70 ";
+        pn = 6;
+    } else if (text[end - 1] == '?') {
+        prefix = "`vb58 ";
+        pn = 6;
+    } else {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    out = (char *)malloc(len + pn + 1);
+    if (out == 0)
+        return 0;
+    memcpy(out, prefix, pn);
+    memcpy(out + pn, text, len);
+    out[pn + len] = 0;
+    *newlen = pn + len;
+    return out;
+}
+
 /* Recode the text if the SSML filter is in the way, and answer whichever
    buffer the caller should go on with. Either of the two out parameters may
    come back holding something that has to be given back afterwards. */
@@ -401,6 +460,7 @@ THIS void addTextRun(SynthThread *t, char *text, uint32_t len, int32_t seq,
